SUMMARY:Wednesday night Bent Creek
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nHard Times Trailhead near Lake Pow
 hatan Rec Area\nWeather: Updated\, No T-Storms are predicted as of Sunday\
 , I'll let you know if it's raining\, and/or cancelled.\nI did this hike s
 eries for many years before 2022\, but I did it as a high-speed hike\, and
  I am now doing it as a moderate speed hike. This is a numbers limited eve
 nt and I expect people who sign-up to show up. Late cancellations\, and th
 ose that don't show up are bumping other interested hikers\, and they will
  not be allowed on future hikes.\nIf all goes well\, I will try to post a 
 hike most weeks\, and for days Tue or Wed\, distance\, and start location\
 , like switching between Hard Times trail-head and Bent Creek River Park\,
  may change.\nThe current route is about 5.5 miles.\nPlease folks\, this i
 s intended as a moderate paced hike\, and we'd like all attendees to keep 
 up with the hike leader(s). This hike is intended as a workout hike for pe
 ople to get in condition to do weekend hikes.\nModerate paced means 22-24 
 min miles\, or 2 ½ mph.\nAs such\, we do not take breaks\, take in views\
 , or snap photos along the way. Please make sure you're able to keep up wi
 th the group. This hike has always served as a good chance to get exercise
  during the week\, meet new people\, and create interest for weekend enjoy
 ment hikes. It's a great introduction to the AHG family.\nNo need to RSVP 
 "No" or "not attending" unless changing from a "Yes."\nPlease read the ful
 l description before RSVPing\, and only sign up if you are sure you can go
 . Thanks in advance for keeping your RSVP up-to-date and not being a last-
 minute cancellation or no-show. This is an ongoing issue with Meetups and 
 often keeps people on waitlists from being able to attend our hikes.\nHard
  Times Trailhead near Lake Powhatan Rec Area\nFollow signs off of Brevard 
 Rd (Rt 191) to Lake Powhatan Rec Area. The road is Bent Creek Ranch Rd. to
  Wesley Branch Rd. Follow signs to Lake Powhatan until you come to Hard Ti
 mes Trailhead on your left\, 2.5 miles. It is very clearly marked. Parking
  is very limited at the trailhead but there’s a paved pull-off just befo
 re the Hard Times trailhead and more parking just beyond at the Ledford Br
 anch trailhead. We will access Bent Creek forest by way of Hard Times Trai
 l and do some combination of loop and out and back.\nArrive at the trailhe
 ad BY 6:00. Because it is a weeknight hike\, we are unable to wait for lat
 ecomers\, fighting daylight.\n\\*\\*\\*If you are running behind\, please 
 post a comment on this Meetup page by 5:45 pm. There is no cell service at
  the parking lot\, so if we don't have any advance notice of you running l
 ate by 5:45\, we can't get any notifications at the trailhead and we will 
 not wait for you.\nWe start the hike at 6:00\, rarely do we get much later
  than that.\n• Wear closed-toed footwear appropriate for hiking. The tra
 il will consist of dirt\, rocks\, roots\, mud and mulch.\n• Bring plenty
  of water.\n• Bring rain gear if a chance of rain is in the forecast.\nH
 eadlamps suggested\n• Dogs on leashes the whole time are welcome. This i
 s an active mountain bike area and it can get messy with dogs running loos
 e among hikers and mountain bikers.\nPlease make sure to keep your RSVP up
 -to-date. You don't want to be "that person" who cancels last minute or no
 -shows and keeps someone from joining in if there's a waitlist. Thanks for
  your consideration - it is appreciated!\nFeel free to post questions not 
 covered in this description in the comments section.\nThanks - we'll see y
 ou on the trail!\nDisclaimer and Release of Liability:\nThis activity invo
 lves hiking on city streets that may have traffic and/or natural trails wi
 th roots\, rocks\, and steep sections. Participants are responsible for th
 eir safety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a voluntee
 r and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only to o
 rganize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you acknowl
 edge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries
 \, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated 
 with this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetu
 p terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315445829
 /
