SUMMARY:Looking Glass Rock - 6 Mi\, 1700 Ft EG
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**DETAILS**\n\n* 6 Miles\, 1700 Fe
 et Elevation Gain so a Moderate level\n* Carpool - 8am at Tanger Outlets p
 arking lot behind the Waffle House (link labeled Asheville Outlets)\, 8:35
  at Pisgah Ranger Station Outer Loop\n* Hike Start - 8:45 at Trailhead htt
 ps://maps.app.goo.gl/3zsHykkoJwRB23neA\n* Sign up starts at 8pm Sunday\, I
  am keeping group small this week.\n\nThis is a busy trail but one that I 
 don't do often enough. The hike departs from the trailhead on Fish Hatcher
 y Road and begins winding its way along switchbacks to the top. This is a 
 gradual ascent. A couple of miles into our hike\, we will come across a fl
 at\, rocky area that is used as a helicopter landing zone for rock climber
 s and hikers needing rescue. We will walk off the main trail here for an a
 mazing view! Next we will stop at the top on the rock for a snack and time
  to absorb the views before heading back down.\n\n**CARPOOL**\nParking can
  be tough so we will start early this week. I want to start hiking by 8:45
  so that means we need to leave the Tanger Outlets by 8am. We will stop by
  the Pisgah Ranger Station at 8:35 and pick up all folks meeting there. Pl
 ease be a little early to each of the carpool stops.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll 
 watch the weather and post a cancellation message by 7:00 AM if the foreca
 st is >50% chance of precipitation.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message me 
 through MeetUp until 8:00 AM the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy\, b
 ut you can try to text or call me up to the start of the hike: (508) 965-2
 333.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking an
 d\, possibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants ar
 e responsible for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropria
 te skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may i
 nvolve risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Ashe
 ville Hiking Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Partici
 pants assume full responsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
